3.  **Step 2: Generalize `gmtime`:**
    *   Find the old overload for 
`std::chrono::time_point<std::chrono::system_clock>`.
    *   Replace it with a templated overload on `Duration`.
    *   Convert `time_point.time_since_epoch()` to seconds using the wrapper.
    *   Call `gmtime(std::time_t)`.
    *   *Old code:*
        ```cpp
        inline std::tm gmtime(
            std::chrono::time_point<std::chrono::system_clock> time_point) {
          return gmtime(std::chrono::system_clock::to_time_t(time_point));
        }
        ```
    *   *New code:*
        ```cpp
        template <typename Duration>
        inline std::tm gmtime(
            std::chrono::time_point<std::chrono::system_clock, Duration> 
time_point) {
          using seconds = std::chrono::seconds;
          auto converted = 
duration_cast_or_error<seconds>(time_point.time_since_epoch());
          return gmtime(static_cast<std::time_t>(converted.count()));
        }
        ```

